{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q407515","formula":"AgBr","hill":"AgBr","elements":["Br","Ag"],"composition":{"Ag":1.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"Silver bromide","ru":"Бромид серебра(I)","uk":"Бромід срібла"},"descriptions":{"en":"Silver bromide (AgBr), a soft, pale-yellow, water-insoluble salt well known (along with other silver halides) for its unusual sensitivity to light. This property has allowed silver halides to become the basis of modern photographic materials. AgBr is widely used in photographic films and is believed by some to have been used for faking the Shroud of Turin.","ru":"Броми́д серебра́ (как минерал также бромит или бромаргирит) — светло-жёлтое кристаллическое вещество, нерастворимое в воде, имеет ионное строение.","uk":"Бромі́д срі́́бла, аргентум бромід — неорганічна сполука, сіль складу AgBr. Має жовтувато-сіре забарвлення, яке дає змогу проводити якісні реакції на вміст бромідів."},"fame":39,"pubchemCid":66199,"mass":187.77,"charge":0,"smiles":"Br[Ag]","inchikey":"ADZWSOLPGZMUMY-UHFFFAOYSA-M","iupac":"bromosilver","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-23231","atoms":27,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[5.784,0.0,0.0],[0.0,5.784,0.0],[0.0,0.0,5.784]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Ag"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":5.784,"el":"Ag"},{"x":0.0,"y":5.784,"z":0.0,"el":"Ag"},{"x":0.0,"y":5.784,"z":5.784,"el":"Ag"},{"x":5.784,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Ag"},{"x":5.784,"y":0.0,"z":5.784,"el":"Ag"},{"x":5.784,"y":5.784,"z":0.0,"el":"Ag"},{"x":5.784,"y":5.784,"z":5.784,"el":"Ag"},{"x":0.0,"y":2.892,"z":0.0,"el":"Br"},{"x":0.0,"y":2.892,"z":5.784,"el":"Br"},{"x":5.784,"y":2.892,"z":0.0,"el":"Br"},{"x":5.784,"y":2.892,"z":5.784,"el":"Br"},{"x":0.0,"y":2.892,"z":2.892,"el":"Ag"},{"x":5.784,"y":2.892,"z":2.892,"el":"Ag"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":2.892,"el"